      "id": 1,
      "text": "South Browning was incorporated in 1912 and named after Daniel M., a local pioneer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://discoveringmontana.com/towns/south-browning/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community sits inside the 1.5‑million‑acre Blackfeet Reservation, the third‑largest in Montana, shaping its land use and economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/south_browning_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "South Browning lies on the eastern edge of Glacier National Park, offering a gateway to the park’s rugged scenery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://discoveringmontana.com/towns/south-browning/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "South Browning serves as the headquarters for the Blackfeet Indian Reservation, making it a cultural and administrative hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://discoveringmontana.com/towns/south-browning/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Museum of the Plains Indians showcases historic clothing, weapons, and art, preserving the region’s indigenous heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://discoveringmontana.com/towns/south-browning/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Chief Mountain, a 6‑mile long peak near South Browning, offers hikers a panoramic view of the surrounding landscape.",
